WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:04.290
- [Woman] This is a destroyed
turret gun of a Russian tank.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.700
It was blown off the vehicle,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.880
and landed in the second
story of a house in Ukraine.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.130
Images from the war show
many tanks ending up,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.170
with this type of damage.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.060
In some cases, the top of the vehicle,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.400
flies a significant distance away.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.370
- We're getting so much
video of these tank losses.

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.560
It's really very illustrative
of what's happening,

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:25.233
in ways that was just
invisible in other wars.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.040
- [Woman] Tanks play a crucial
role in ground warfare,

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.020
and as the world's
second largest exporter,

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.520
of military equipment,

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.440
Russian made vehicles
are used in countries,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.783
including India, Iran, and Algeria.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.510
But hundreds have been destroyed,

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.070
during the war with Ukraine.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.600
In what military analysts say,

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.520
could be the biggest
loss of Russian tanks,

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.110
since World War II.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.760
- [Jeffrey] It's gonna be
the better part of a decade,

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.710
before they're actually able
to get their force back,

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.450
to where they were.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.490
- [Woman] The ongoing war
has put this vulnerability,

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.810
on public display.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.820
Complicating Russia's campaign in Ukraine,

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.533
and its production of tanks.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:02.670
While Moscow hasn't said
how many of its tanks,

00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.920
have been destroyed since
the start of the war,

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.310
at least 440 have been
documented by Oryx Blog,

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.980
an open source military equipment tracker.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:13.480
More than half of these
are the same type of tank.

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:17.700
To understand why we need
to look at their design.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.460
The T-72 was first produced in 1969,

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.890
with many design iterations since.

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.720
One of its most distinctive features,

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:26.670
is also a vulnerability.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:29.040
This is the auto-loading mechanism.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.470
It reduces the crew from
four to three members,

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.370
by removing the person responsible
for loading the main gun.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.800
Most of the ammunition
for this auto loader,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.480
is stored in the carousel,

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.570
a kind of metal basket that
the gunner sits on top of,

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.730
the rest is often stored
in nooks and crannies,

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.980
around the inside of the tank.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.110
Having these elements
stacked on top of each other,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:53.910
save space within the T-72
and gives it a low profile.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:56.100
- It makes it much harder
to see from the side,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.510
makes it harder to hit.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:58.920
- [Woman] William Albert is a director,

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.240
at the London based Think Tank,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.853
the International Institute
for Strategic Studies.

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:05.790
He studied arms control and disarmament,

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.770
for more than two decades.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.980
- Early tanks tended to
be relatively tall things.

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:12.990
It'd be relatively easy for a soldier,

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.800
with an anti tank missile to
take it out from a distance,

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:18.120
because the higher it is, you know,

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:21.930
you can hit the turret
from quite a ways away.

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.910
- [Woman] The compact
design has made the T-72,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.220
a cost effective and popular tank,

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:28.773
with thousands used by
militaries around the world.

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.190
But this design comes with a drawback.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.970
What military analysts call
the Jack-in-the-Box Effect.

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.920
That can happen when
the explosive material,

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.330
makes its way into the tank,

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.430
usually through the turret ring.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:44.640
In a T-72, this sparks a chain reaction.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:46.530
The fire sets off the spare ammunition,

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:48.570
stored around the inside of the tank,

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.950
which in turn, sets off the rest,

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.870
that's stored underneath the crew.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:52.890
If the hatch is sealed,

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.750
the resulting explosion is pressurized,

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.220
underneath the turret.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.830
And this video filmed by
a Chinese television crew,

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.010
in Ukraine, shows what can happen next.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.840
- Gas builds up. The explosive builds up.

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.490
And it sends the turrets sky
high. Sometimes meters high.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:11.220
- [Woman] Modern Western tanks,
like the American M1 Abrams,

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.810
have avoided this design.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:15.420
Instead storing ammunition
behind an armored wall,

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.710
in the back.

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.320
This design makes it
taller and easier to hit.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:22.740
But if the ammunition is set
off, it has a safer outlet.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.440
- And so the ammunition goes
out the back of the turret,

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:26.640
and doesn't kill the crew,

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.650
and they used to make us watch
videos and things like that,

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:31.020
just to reassure us
that that was the case.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.730
- [Woman] Jeffrey Edmonds
served in the US Army,

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:36.450
for more than 20 years with
tours in Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.920
He's now a research scientist,

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:39.960
with the Center for Naval Analysis.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.270
A nonprofit organization
that provides research,

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:43.683
for the US Military.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:48.090
Edmonds says the T-72's
weaknesses were amplified,

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:50.490
by Russia's strategy for
how the tanks were deployed,

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.570
in Ukraine.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.460
Footage released by
the Ukrainian military,

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.970
shows Russian tanks driving
in convoys towards Kiev.

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.100
- [Jeffrey] You don't just
drive tanks down roads,

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:04.100
and columns, when there's a
threat of anti-tank missiles,

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.120
or mines or things of that nature.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:08.160
- [Woman] This initial push
left the vehicles exposed,

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:09.210
to Ukrainian soldiers,

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.460
armed with thousands of
high-powered missiles,

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:13.080
that have been effective at triggering,

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:14.940
the Jack-in-the-Box Effect.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:15.930
- [Jeffrey] When you look at the modern,

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.450
javelin type weapons or the in-laws,

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:20.790
you have basically, explosion
coming from the top,

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.820
and typically tanks have very
little protection on the top.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.660
And so when that happens,

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.150
that's the second way you
could get explosive material,

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.150
inside the crew compartment
that can set the ammunition off.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:32.340
- [Woman] But as the war has shifted away,

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:35.670
from urban centers towards the
Donbas region of the country,

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.460
battles are now taking
place on open fields,

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.040
giving Russia's tanks
more of an advantage.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.750
- [Jeffrey] The fight in the
east is a different fight.

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:45.540
It's characterized much
more by artillery duals.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:47.340
And that's why I think the Ukrainians,

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.710
are suffering more
casualties now than they did,

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:51.240
at the beginning.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.500
- [Woman] Russia's Ministry of Defense,

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.240
didn't respond to a request for comment,

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.840
about the design of its tanks
or how they were deployed.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.750
Ukraine has also been using
the same Russian made tanks.

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.130
The military analysts say,

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:04.410
it's seen comparatively fewer losses.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:08.070
In part by attempting to minimize
the tanks vulnerabilities.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:12.813
- In some cases that means
going in with fewer rounds,

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:17.070
and not storing as much
of the powdered charges,

00:05:17.070 --> 00:05:20.643
inside, haphazardly within the
tank that the Russians are.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.400
- [Woman] All this
could create challenges,

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.380
for Russia's weapons industry.

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:28.080
The vulnerabilities of the
T-72 are being displayed,

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.300
to tank operators in
other countries watching,

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.280
what's happening in Ukraine.

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:34.770
- It's gotta be a little
bit terrifying now to be,

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.320
you know, a tanker in a
country that has T-72s.

00:05:37.320 --> 00:05:42.000
And to think that you are
stepping into a system,

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.960
whose design choice was
that if the tank is tough.

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:46.890
- [Woman] Western sanctions,

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.410
have also limited Russia's
access to microchips,

00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.910
and advanced circuitry.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.400
Stifling their capacity
to develop and produce,

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.260
newer tanks and missiles.

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.120
- [Jeffrey] I think that's
gonna continue being a problem,

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.560
for their more advanced systems.

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.630
And with everything else
happening with, you know,

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:03.870
young, tech savvy people
leaving sanctions,

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:05.280
you know, the economic downturn,

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:06.780
mid to long term that's... (stammers)

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:07.833
It's pretty bleep.

